                  <article class="doc">
                    <h4>Rounding</h4>
                    <p>
                      Money is stored in minor units: cents, pence, yen. Every amount that reaches the
                      <a>Ledger</a> is already an integer, so rounding happens before a value is written,
                      never after.
                    </p>
                    <h5>Where it happens</h5>
                    <p class="doc__changed">
                      <span class="doc__gone">Each invoice line rounds its own total.</span>
                      <span class="doc__insert"
                        ><span class="doc__typed">Rounding happens once, in the ledger, using half to even. Invoices pass exact totals and let the ledger round them, so a long invoice no longer drifts a cent per line.</span
                        ><span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cursor__flag">Claude</span></span
                        ><span class="doc__rest"></span
                      ></span>
                    </p>
                    <h5>Why half to even</h5>
                    <p>
                      Rounding half up nudges totals upward across many entries. Half to even matches
                      how existing entries were written, which <a>Reconciliation</a> depends on.
                    </p>
                  </article>
                  <div class="cbar">
                    <span class="cbar__count">1 agent change</span>
                    <span class="cbar__btn">Previous</span>
                    <span class="cbar__btn">Next</span>
                    <span class="cbar__btn">Accept all</span>
                    <span class="cbar__btn">Revert all</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </figure>
              </div>
              <div class="surface__desc">
                <p>
                  Ask Claude to bring a page up to date and you watch it edit: its words tinted, what it
                  removes ghosted, its cursor named. Your own edits wait until its turn finishes, so neither
                  overwrites the other.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Each edit lands as an amendment in a pull request, and you can revert any one on its own.
                  The wiki changes only when a person merges.
                </p>
                <p class="surface__note">
                  Agents edit through the app’s wiki tools, none of which can merge. Verified with Claude Code
                  today; any agent that calls Astrolabe’s wiki tools can use them.
                </p>
