              <div class="surface__desc">
                <p>
                  A link can say what it means. Write its type into the link itself, and the Ledger note
                  says it depends on Rounding:
                  <code class="surface__code">[[Rounding|rounding @depends-on]]</code>
                  The type reads as a mark beside the words and stays in the Markdown.
                </p>
                <p>
                  A base is a live filter over the wiki that reads those typed links. This one lists every
                  note that links to Rounding as depends-on or decided-in. People run it before changing a
                  core invariant, and agent skills query it at runtime to pull only the knowledge a specific
                  workflow needs.
                </p>
                <p class="surface__note">
                  Bases use Obsidian’s format, so a base written in Obsidian works here. Obsidian keeps typed
                  links working, but its bases can’t read the types.
                </p>
